  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Fair weather this weekend will give way to more\nunsettled weather into early next week.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nPatchy river valley fog is developing this morning in areas that\nsaw rain yesterday and where winds have decoupled. NW winds \nwill occasionally gust to between 20-25kts on the higher terrain\nthis afternoon with fairly tight pressure gradient remaining \nbetween exiting low pressure over the Maritimes and building \nhigh pressure over the Great Lakes. As the high builds in skies\nwill clear overnight and winds begin to decouple with another\nround of patchy river valley fog expected late tonight into\nSaturday morning. \n\nHigh pressure builds in through weekend, with drier weather and\ncooler temperatures returning to the forecast area. High \ntemperatures each day may only lift into the 70s, and skies \ncould remain mostly sunny on Saturday. By Sunday, cloud cover \nmay begin to increase once more ahead of the next approaching \nlow pressure system, though there is the possibility this system\ncould slow upon approach, delaying the onset of mostly cloudy \nskies to early next week.\n\nThe next low pressure system to cross the area early next week \nwill be in the form of a cold front which brings another round \nof rain and chance for thunderstorms. Current trends suggest \nshowers will remain scattered along the boundary as they move \nthrough as there will be a lack of deep moisture support, but if\nthe trough deepens more and reaches further into the Gulf, \nthere could be more numerous showers and storms due to the \nsynoptic forcing of the cold front.",
